</section>
</section>
<section id="S5" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">5 </span>Conclusion</h2>

<div id="S5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this paper, we propose <span id="S5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">TurboVSR</span>, an diffusion based video super-resolution model with ultra efficient designs.
We provide three key technical contributions: high compression ratio autoencoder for reducing tokens; factorized conditioning for easy convergence; and non-uniform shortcut model for fewer-step sampling.
Compared with existing diffusion-based VSR models, we reduce the computation cost by 100+ times, while results on benchmarks are still comparable. We hope our design, especially the usage of high compression ration autoencoder, to inspire future research in this direction.</p>
</div>
</section>
